Corrective provider-catalog decision record (2026-08-29)

Root cause:
- claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 and qwen3.8-flash were intended only as bounded live-validation targets.
- The implementation incorrectly promoted those two IDs into product allowlists: RouteProfile.strict_model_allowlist filtered the shared remote catalog, the native Anthropic parser independently kept only Haiku, and the Anthropic payload builder assumed the Haiku manual-thinking contract for every Claude model.

Decisions:
- Account/provider model catalogs are the availability authority. Every valid Anthropic model returned by GET /v1/models is retained; every Qwen chat model returned by the configured Model Studio catalog is retained after the existing bounded chat-model classifier.
- Remote lists remain bounded to 500 models and deduplicated. Known non-chat families stay excluded from the chat selector.
- Embedded anthropic.json and qwen.json entries are enrichment and outage fallback evidence, never allowlists. A successful catalog without either live-test model remains usable.
- Anthropic native capability fields drive tools, image input, thinking types, effort modes and output/input limits. Null or zero limits mean unpublished and no longer reject the full catalog.
- Claude models publishing adaptive thinking use thinking.type=adaptive and output_config.effort. Haiku 4.5 retains manual enabled-thinking budgets. Unsupported reasoning modes fail closed.
- The now single-purpose strict_model_allowlist field was removed instead of leaving a dormant second authority.

Regression coverage:
- Anthropic catalog keeps Haiku plus another Claude model and preserves native capability metadata.
- Anthropic successful catalog without Haiku stays usable.
- Anthropic zero limits do not cause fallback to the single embedded model.
- Qwen catalog keeps qwen3.8-max plus qwen3.8-flash and remains usable without the test model.
- Adaptive Anthropic payload shape is asserted with supported-mode guards.

